#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:0
msgid ""
"Configure Orca key bindings, including the Orca Modifier keys, the key "
"bindings table and unbound commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:7
msgid "Key bindings preferences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:9
msgid "Orca Modifier Keys"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:11
msgid ""
"The Screen Reader Modifier Key(s) combo box allows you to select which key "
"or keys will serve as the Orca Modifier. The available options are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:13
msgid "KP_Insert (the same key as the {kbd}`0` on the numeric keypad)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:15
msgid "Insert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:17
msgid "Insert, KP_Insert"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:19
msgid "Caps_Lock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:21
msgid "Key bindings table"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:23
msgid ""
"The key bindings table provides a list of Orca operations and the keys that "
"are bound to them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:25
msgid ""
"The **Command** column contains a description of the Orca command to be "
"performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:27
msgid ""
"The **Key Binding** column contains the keyboard shortcut currently assigned "
"to the Orca command. You can modify the value of this column by pressing "
"{kbd}`Return`, pressing the keys for the new binding, and pressing {kbd}"
"`Return` again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:29
msgid ""
"The **Modified** column serves both as an indicator to what has been changed "
"and as a way to restore the default bindings associated with that command."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:31
msgid "Unbound commands"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/accessibility/orca-preferences/orca-preferences-key-binding.md:33
msgid ""
"Beneath the list of Orca keybindings, you will find a group of unbound "
"commands. These are commands can be useful for some users but are unassigned "
"by default.  Braille bindings are listed at the bottom of unbound commands "
"list."
msgstr ""
